    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the sole concrete test `AcceptanceTest` passing, including the new `coreIdempotentRepeat` case).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe request can now carry an `Idempotency-Key` header on `POST /api/owners`. A repeat with an already-seen key replays the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which otherwise would 409 on identity).\n\nI followed the project's OfficeFloor conventions \u2014 small function classes wired in YAML, escalation-based error handling (the proven mechanism, rather than the never-used `@Flow`), and `Out<T>`/`@Val` for state:\n\n**New pipeline steps** in `owners.POST.yml`:\n- `checkIdempotency` (new **first** step, before any validation/duplicate check) \u2014 reads the optional header via Spring MVC's `@RequestHeader(required=false)`, publishes it as an `Out<IdempotencyKey>` variable, and if the key was already seen throws a checked `IdempotentReplayException` to short-circuit the pipeline.\n- `recordIdempotency` (inserted after `audit`, before `respond`, under the same `transaction` governance) \u2014 records `key \u2192 new owner id` once the create succeeds and the id is assigned.\n\n**New classes:**\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a `@Component` singleton holding an in-memory `key \u2192 ownerId` map (`putIfAbsent`, so first-seen wins).\n- `IdempotencyKey` \u2014 a small wrapper so the pipeline variable is unambiguous (vs. a bare `String`).\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey`, `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 the two step functions.\n- `IdempotentReplayException` + `IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler` (with `escalation/\u2026IdempotentReplayException.yml`) \u2014 the handler loads the recorded owner and responds `ResponseEntity.ok(dto)` \u2192 200.\n\nA create without the header is unaffected: `checkIdempotency` publishes an absent key, proceeds normally, and `recordIdempotency` no-ops.\n\nOne note on scope: the store is unbounded in-memory (no eviction/TTL) and records within the write transaction rather than strictly post-commit \u2014 fine for this endpoint and the tests, but worth revisiting if this needs to survive restarts or run multi-instance.",
