    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered account of what happens on `POST /api/owners` (fully-qualified route is actually `POST /petclinic/api/owners` given the `server.servlet.context-path`). The endpoint is a linear OfficeFloor pipeline \u2014 23 steps, no branches; every rejection is a thrown checked exception mapped to an HTTP status by an escalation handler.\n\nI'll mark each as **[V]** validation (can reject the request) or **[S]** side-effect (mutation, write, or emission).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n0. **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` evaluated inline. Denial \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` \u2192 **403**.\n\n## Pre-transaction steps (run outside the `transaction` governance)\n1. **[S/V] CheckIdempotencyKey** \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header; publishes it as a pipeline variable. If a non-blank key was already recorded from a prior successful create, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 handler reloads that owner and returns **200** (replay, no new owner created).\n2. **[V+S] ValidateOwnerFields** \u2014 binds the `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (the only body read). **Side-effects:** normalizes `addressLine1/2` and `address` via `AddressNormalizer` (trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand ST\u2192STREET/RD\u2192ROAD/AVE\u2192AVENUE); composes flat `address` from `addressLine1(+addressLine2)` when present. **Validation:** requires non-blank `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone`; missing ones \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (carries the field list) \u2192 **400**.\n3. **[V] ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 only when postcode present: must be exactly 4 digits; if `CityRegion.postcodeRange(city)` is known, value must fall in that range. Else \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n4. **[V] ValidateRegistrationDate** \u2014 only when a `registrationDate` is supplied: must not be after `LocalDate.now()`. Else \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**.\n5. **[S/V] NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 rewrites telephone to E.164 via `E164Telephone.normalize` (strips separators; defaults no-plus numbers to `+61`/AU, stripping a leading 0; enforces 8\u201315 digits and per-country national length for +61/+1). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400**.\n6. **[S/V] NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 only when email present: must match the email regex; on success trims and lower-cases it. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 **400**.\n7. **[V] RejectDisposableEmailDomain** \u2014 only when email present: domain must not be in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Blocked \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` \u2192 **400**.\n8. **[S] ResolveRegistrationDate** \u2014 computes the effective registration date (supplied, or `LocalDate.now()`), then rolls it forward off Saturdays, Sundays, and the 2026 public-holiday set; publishes it as a `LocalDate` variable. (No rejection.)\n\n## Transactional steps (`govern: [ transaction ]`, steps 9\u201323 \u2014 commit once at the end)\n9. **[V] EnsureCityCapacity** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n10. **[V] EnsureDailyLimit** \u2014 counts existing owners whose registrationDate equals the resolved date; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyLimitReachedException` \u2192 **429**.\n11. **[S] BuildOwner** \u2014 maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`); publishes it.\n12. **[S] AssignHousehold** \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 6 bytes of SHA-256 of `normalized(lastName)|postcode` (null when postcode blank).\n13. **[V] EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 against non-deleted existing owners: unless `sharesHousehold` is true, a matching `householdId` is a collision; and a matching whole identity key (`normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`) is a collision \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n14. **[S] FlagPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`: flags (does not reject) when a non-deleted owner shares last name + postcode but has a different telephone (skipped if `sharesHousehold`); picks the lowest-id match.\n15. **[S] AssignHouseholdSize** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = 1 + count of existing owners sharing the `householdId` (1 when no householdId).\n16. **[S] DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 writes the resolved `registrationDate` onto the entity.\n17. **[S] AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 computes `CustomerCode.of(region, telephone, lastName)` and de-duplicates against existing codes by appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 ; sets `customerCode`.\n18. **[S] AssignNamesakeCount** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n19. **[S] AssignBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when > 80 existing owners share the resolved registration date.\n20. **[S] SaveOwner** \u2014 persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n21. **[S] AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membership level, derived membership number).\n22. **[S] RecordIdempotencyKey** \u2014 if a key was supplied, records `key \u2192 new owner id` in the `IdempotencyStore` (so future repeats replay per step 1).\n23. **[S] RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 maps the entity to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- **Two validation layers coexist.** The pipeline does all the checks above *imperatively*. Separately, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` carries JSR-380 annotations (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size`, `@Email`, e.g. `telephone` must match `^[0-9]*$`). If bean-validation runs on binding, a `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 `ValidationExceptionHandler` \u2192 **400** is a possible earlier rejection path. Note the DTO's telephone `@Pattern(^[0-9]*$)` conflicts with the pipeline accepting `+`/spaces/dashes \u2014 worth being aware of, though you asked me only to read, not to change anything.\n- **Ordering is deliberate** (per the YAML comments): validation/normalization before build; capacity/limit counted on the *resolved* business day; identity uniqueness checked *after* `householdId` is assigned; idempotency replay short-circuits before any of it.\n- **Transaction boundary:** steps 1\u20138 run outside the transaction; the first repository read (step 9) through the response (step 23) run under `transaction` governance and commit once."
